SplitReason is an online t-shirt store that gives it's affiliates a 23.5%
commission on any shirt purchased through them. The typical price is
~US$18, so that's $4 for the LLG per shirt. I haven't done the math, but I
think that's slightly better:

http://www.splitreason.com/info/affiliate

On Fri, Jun 29, 2012 at 3:25 AM, la .lindar. <lindarthebard@gmail.com>wrote:

> So, we're looking into who can produce our merchandise. The biggest
> problem seems to be how much we have to charge. The *cheapest* we've seen
> for individual (read: non-bulk) orders is 15$ for a plain white shirt with
> a design. So, to make any kind of money, we'd have to mark it up. That
> brings it to... let's just say 20$. Now unless you  surpass some number
> (around 50?) of dollars on your order you'll also end up paying shipping,
> which we'll laughably say 5$ even though that could vary a lot in either
> direction.
>
> So,  somebody is paying 25$ for a shirt and we're making 5$ off of it.
> That doesn't seem fair for the buyer or us.
>
> Suggestions?
